  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias during high volatility regimes; forecasts consistently overestimate the immediate post-spike correction phase by 15-20%.",
    "When sentiment history shows a recent spike (e.g., >0.25) followed by neutralization, the model fails to account for mean reversion and instead projects a linear continuation of the prior trend.",
    "Forecasts are systematically lagged in recognizing sharp downward reversals; the model assumes stability after a drop while true outcomes show immediate further declines before recovery.",
    "In periods of high sentiment volatility (sentiment variance > 0.15), reduce forecast confidence by 30% and apply a mean-reversion coefficient to the last 7 days of price history.",
    "The model ignores the 'V-shape' recovery pattern common in EU ETS; it predicts a smooth linear rebound from lows, whereas true outcomes often show extended consolidation or secondary dips before rising."
  ]
}
